            <ArticleTitle>[Rupture of rudimentary horn pregnancy at the 18th week of gestation: a case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>505-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of pregnancy in a rudimentary horn that ruptured at 18 weeks. An emergency laparotomy was taken for acute abdomen and ruptured right rudimentary horn pregnancy was diagnosed. Excision of the rudimentary horn and ipsilateral salpingectomy were carried out. The patient's postoperative course was uneventful, and she left the hospital 6 days later.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
